# L §4.4 windows each on a line that reaches an axis (L §5.5: every combination of the axes the line reads is
# evaluated; one line per distinct result).  Under mode a the cutoff is 07-05: d < cutoff is true on 07-01 .. 07-04;
# under b it is 07-08: true on 07-01 .. 07-07.  The combinations' sub-window lines differ, so each is printed with
# its option (layout: the window part, then the axis part; `reading:` per L §8.2).  q2 reaches no axis.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

axis mode
  a "first reading"
  b "second reading"

input d: date
input cut_a: date
input cut_b: date

def cutoff: date at reader
  rule base = cut_a
  rule alt beats base = cut_b when mode == b

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  d = window(2020-07-01, 2020-07-10)
  cut_a = 2020-07-05
  cut_b = 2020-07-08

ask q1: d < cutoff law 2026-06-30 windows each
ask q2: d < cut_a law 2026-06-30 windows each
=== expect
q1 [d = 2020-07-01 .. 2020-07-04] [mode = a]: true
  reading: mode = a
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
q1 [d = 2020-07-05 .. 2020-07-10] [mode = a]: false
  reading: mode = a
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
q1 [d = 2020-07-01 .. 2020-07-07] [mode = b]: true
  reading: mode = b
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
q1 [d = 2020-07-08 .. 2020-07-10] [mode = b]: false
  reading: mode = b
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
q2 [d = 2020-07-01 .. 2020-07-04]: true
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
q2 [d = 2020-07-05 .. 2020-07-10]: false
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
